### Sample requests (VS Code "REST Client" or IntelliJ HTTP client). Mock SAP backend on port 8080.
@base = http://localhost:8080

### Health (includes "sap" component)
GET {{base}}/actuator/health

### Create document metadata (internal numbering)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/documents
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cad-job-4711
Idempotency-Key: cad-job-4711

{
  "documentType": "DRW",
  "documentPart": "000",
  "documentVersion": "00",
  "description": "Brake caliper drawing",
  "descriptions": [ { "languageIso": "DE", "description": "Bremssattel Zeichnung" } ],
  "objectLinks":  [ { "objectType": "MARA", "objectKey": "MAT-4711" } ]
}

### Same Idempotency-Key again -> 200, "replayed": true, no second document
POST {{base}}/api/v1/documents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: cad-job-4711

{ "documentType": "DRW", "description": "Brake caliper drawing" }

### Validation error -> 400 with errors[]
POST {{base}}/api/v1/documents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "documentType": "drawing", "description": "" }

### SAP business error (unknown type in mock) -> 422 with sapMessages[]
POST {{base}}/api/v1/documents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "documentType": "ZZZ", "description": "Unknown type" }

### Read metadata (use the number returned above)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/documents/DRW/10000001/000/00

### Upload a PDF original
POST {{base}}/api/v1/documents/DRW/10000001/000/00/originals
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BOUNDARY

--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="caliper.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

%PDF-1.7
%%EOF
--BOUNDARY--

### List originals
GET {{base}}/api/v1/documents/DRW/10000001/000/00/originals

### Download an original (use fileId from the upload response)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/documents/DRW/10000001/000/00/originals/REPLACE-WITH-FILE-ID

### Transaction status (use transactionId from a create response)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/transactions/REPLACE-WITH-TRANSACTION-ID
